{"format_version":"vbulletin-3+-thread","url":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/532278-how-do-sun-and-moon-interact","id":532278,"title":"how do sun and moon interact","path":["Home","Onyx Path","White Wolf Worlds","Chronicles of Darkness","Changeling: The Lost"],"posts":[{"date":"2015-05-29T14:32:02-07:00","id":532278,"title":"how do sun and moon interact","content":"So I am gearing up for my Sun/Moon court game. Ive been using seasonal courts but decided to shake things up a bit, and never really ran a whole lot of court intrigue. <br /> <br /> I guess my mind is so readily accustomed to 1 court being in power at any given time with transitions only happening every 3 months and some dissension on courtly decisions and so on. But the Dynamic of Sun/Moon is so different that I am having some issues figuring out how they would interact... <br /> <br /> It makes sense to me that the two would keep separate freeholds and not associate with one another on a daily basis, but only when absolutely necessary.<br /> <br /> My mind seems stuck on the idea that the two would shift power at sunrise/sunset every day, but that line of thinking seems to eliminate A LOT of intrigue and plot potential<br /> <br /> It was suggested to me that a courts power waxes and wains on the highpoint of their respective celestial bodies. But this idea seems too mechanically clunky to me and allows for too much weird grey area.<br /> <br /> One idea I had was to not have time prescribed as to when their powers transition at all, and that the use of Sun/Moon, Day/Night, Light/Dark to be more philosophically represented. Meaning, both courts maintain power throughout the day, and really only have jurisdiction over their own constituents and their own turf areas. While their activities might primarily be focused in their respective times, they could act freely all day/night long.<br /> <br /> Does anyone have experience in this area? What worked best? One of these, or is there another option I have not considered? What minimum rules would exist between the two to help keep the peace?<br /> <br /> Any suggestions observations or thoughts would be of immense help.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/5989-druidspath","name":"druidspath","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"21"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T00:47:17-07:00","id":534133,"title":"","content":"Main thing is that Courts rule during 12 hours of their respective time-Sun Court, or Day Court, rules through day, and Moon/Night Court rules through night.<br /> They do live in same Freehold-just like Seasonal Courts. Thing that makes their interaction interesting is this: During time of one's rule, other Court submits to their laws but works from shadows to undermine their efforts.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6005-coolcat12345","name":"coolcat12345","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T16:36:44-07:00","id":534941,"title":"","content":"Pretty much as coolcat said. They switch on a clock basis.","signature":"<hr class=\"b-divider\"/><br/><img itemprop=\"image\" class=\"bbcode-attachment\" src=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/OnyxGraphics/OnyxMod.png\" border=\"0\" alt=\"\" /><span style=\"color:#FF0000\">Onyx Path Moderator </span><br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/onyx-path-announcements/206-forum-rules\" target=\"_blank\">Forum Rules</a><br /> <span style=\"color:#FF0000\">This is my mod voice.</span> This is my goth voice.<br /> <a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/geist-the-sin-eaters/15731-geist-balance-of-shadows-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">[Geist: Balance of Shadows</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-classic-world-of-darkness/vampire-the-masquerade/17537-v20-the-conspiracy-of-hrad-%C4%8Dern%C3%A1-hora-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Vampire: The Conspiracy of Hrad \u010cern\u00e1 Hora</a><a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/scion/13838-scion-bohemian-front-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\"> ][ Scion: Bohemian Front</a>][<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/99033-changeling-malibu-dream-house-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Changeling: Malibu Dream House</a>] [<a href=\"http://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/demon-the-descent/268069-demon-night-train-detective-agency-actual-play\" target=\"_blank\">Demon: Night Train Detective Agency</a>] <a href=\"http://tinyurl.com/la94fvk\" target=\"_blank\">[WoD: The Golden Eagle</a>]","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/56-baroness-nerak","name":"Baroness Nerak","avatar":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/core/avatars/0/0/6/0/4/5/avatar56_2.jpeg","title":"Moderator","rank":6,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Oct 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"2524"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T16:55:33-07:00","id":534951,"title":"","content":"The Night Watch books would probably be pretty good inspiration.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/1059-azahul","name":"Azahul","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"1465"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-05-31T18:27:51-07:00","id":534994,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>coolcat12345</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/532278-how-do-sun-and-moon-interact?p=534133#post534133\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"> Thing that makes their interaction interesting is this: During time of one's rule, other Court submits to their laws but works from shadows to undermine their efforts.</div> </div> </div> </div>This. One of the big features of the Sun/Moon courts is how adversarial their relationship is. A lot of their material has really played on this, and it's one of the cooler things about them; at best, a freehold divided between these two courts is an argument away from open warfare. Now, this is pure fanon, but you've got to wonder how successful that is against the gentry- the court systems work because they're about sharing power. Sun and Moon have real trouble doing that.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[{"type":"\ud83d\udc4d","count":2}],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/768-djehuty3","name":"djehuty3","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"Nov 2013"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"56"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T14:00:20-07:00","id":535909,"title":"","content":"Things you have to remember in campaign with them:<br /> <b>Opposition: </b>they are completely opposed. Not just in political way, but conceptual and every else. They are possibly reason why phrase ''different like day and night'' exists.<br /> <b>Balance: </b>One Court may have edge for some time, but in end they're always equal. When one gains something, other seeks to either find similar or destroy whatever they gained. This is somehow result of above.<br /> <b>Shadow work: </b>fitting-shadow is born of light and dark. Because they are, as djehuty pointed out, inch away from open warfare, they hate each other, and spiral into whirlwind of sabotage and backstabbing that would make elder Kindred's jaw fall to floor. As we Slavs tend to say it, public secret-everybody knows that happened, but cannot say because of consequences.<br />","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6005-coolcat12345","name":"coolcat12345","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]},{"date":"2015-06-01T14:01:56-07:00","id":535910,"title":"","content":"<div class=\"bbcode_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote\"> <div class=\"quote_container\"> <div class=\"bbcode_quote_container b-icon b-icon__ldquo-l--gray\"></div> <div class=\"bbcode_postedby\"> Originally posted by <strong>djehuty3</strong> <a href=\"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/forum/main-category/main-forum/the-new-world-of-darkness/changeling-the-lost/532278-how-do-sun-and-moon-interact?p=534994#post534994\" rel=\"nofollow\" title=\"View Post\" class=\"b-icon b-icon__double-arrow-right--blue animate-scroll\">View Post</a> </div> <div class=\"message\"><br /> This. Now, this is pure fanon, but you've got to wonder how successful that is against the gentry- the court systems work because they're about sharing power. Sun and Moon have real trouble doing that.</div> </div> </div> </div>Also pure fanon-they hate each other, are completely different, yet they don't war and submit to laws of other Court during their time. True Fae cannot comprehend why.","signature":"","edited":{"userid":0,"user_link":"","user":"","date":""},"attachments":[],"reactions":[],"user":{"link":"https://forum.theonyxpath.com/member/6005-coolcat12345","name":"coolcat12345","avatar":"data:image/svg+xml;base64,","title":"Member","rank":0,"rank-name":"","custom":[{"key":"Join Date:","value":"May 2015"},{"key":"Posts:","value":"31"}]},"thankedby":[]}]}